{"name":"Sweet Georgia Brown","hex":"#8b715a","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sweet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tasting of sugars.","Retaining a portion of sugar."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Used as a positive response to good news or information."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweet"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sweet Georgia Brown","blocks":[{"text":"\"Sweet Georgia Brown\" is a jazz standard composed in 1925 by Ben Bernie and Maceo Pinkard, with lyrics by Kenneth Casey."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Sweet_Georgia_Brown_Tempo_Lable_Recorded_by_Brother_Bones_and_His_Shadows.PNG/330px-Sweet_Georgia_Brown_Tempo_Lable_Recorded_by_Brother_Bones_and_His_Shadows.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweet_Georgia_Brown"},{"title":"Sweet Georgia Brown (wrestler)","blocks":[{"text":"Susie Mae McCoy , better known by her ring name Sweet Georgia Brown, was an African-American female professional wrestler who was recognized as the first Black woman to win a title in professional wrestling history."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/34/Sweet_Georgia_Brown_%28wrestler%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweet_Georgia_Brown_(wrestler)"},{"title":"Sweetness","blocks":[{"text":"Sweetness is a basic taste most commonly perceived when eating foods rich in sugar. Sweet tastes are generally regarded as pleasurable. In addition to sugars like sucrose, many other chemical compounds are sweet,